# tools/mycelium_pledge_witness.rish — the Pledge: a two-phase transfer decided by the order (r1).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) · Mycelium consensus · the two-phase transfer verdict · rung r1 — the crux.
# Every Mycelium ledger before this settled a transfer in ONE committed fact. The Pledge settles across TWO:
# coins are reserved now (a pledge), and THEN either honored (a post) or released (a void), so a real trade
# either wholly commits or wholly reverses — TigerBeetle's two-phase transfer, read as the agreed order's law.
#
# The crux this witness proves is EQUIVOCATION: a holder signs BOTH a post and a void for one pledge at the
# same round. No arrival may leave the pledge both honored and released, and no two honest nodes may disagree
# on which won. The Cord's total order is deterministic regardless of arrival, so the FIRST resolution the order
# places decides and the second is a lawful no-op — the same verdict for every honest hand. Conservation is the
# Purse's law widened by one column: at every step the sum of spendable BALANCES plus RESERVED holdings equals
# exactly what genesis issued (a pledge moves coins balance->reserved, a post reserved->recipient, a void
# reserved->balance). A pledge past current balance yet once affordable is a lawful no-op; a post/void of an
# unknown or wrong-signed or amount-mismatched pledge, a reused id, a star reservation, and a malformed body each
# refuse whole. Composes cord + fold + kumara public API only; every buffer bounded; demo keeper seeds — no key,
# no funds, no network, no custody.
#
# Scope: active-designing/20260813-075049_mycelium-pledge-two-phase-transfer-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/mycelium_pledge_witness.rish

say "mycelium-pledge: Language EN — coins held in a promise, and one order to decide whether the promise is kept or let go, never both."
say "mycelium-pledge: Style Radiant — the Purse forgives what a holder took in; the Pledge holds what a holder set aside, and the Cord decides its fate once, plainly, for every hand alike."
say "mycelium-pledge: Lens TAME — the verdict composes cord + fold + kumara public API; every buffer bounded; conservation of balance + reserved holds; an already-settled pledge is a lawful no-op, unknown/wrong-signer/amount-mismatch/star refuse whole; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/pledge"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/pledge.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-pledge: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-pledge: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-pledge: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "one order decides once" else "mycelium-pledge: two-phase decided-once verdict claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "every honest arrival names the same verdict" else "mycelium-pledge: arrival-order-independence claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "conservation of balance + reserved" else "mycelium-pledge: conservation claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "refuse whole" else "mycelium-pledge: refusal claim missing"

# The Cord whose agreed order the Pledge reads, and the Mycelium fold whose signed-fact model and additive
# verify_fact it reuses, both stand at the door — their own selftests prove the machinery the verdict rests on.
let cord = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/cord.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/cord && mycelium/bin/cord 2>&1"]
assert cord.ok else "mycelium-pledge: the Cord the Pledge reads is not GREEN"
assert cord.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-pledge: the Cord did not speak its GREEN"

let fold = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/fold.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/fold && mycelium/bin/fold 2>&1"]
assert fold.ok else "mycelium-pledge: the Mycelium fold the Pledge reuses is not GREEN"
assert fold.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-pledge: the Mycelium fold did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-pledge: GREEN — a pledge reserves coins, one order decides once whether they are honored or released and every honest arrival names the same verdict; conservation of balance + reserved holds against genesis, an open pledge holds coins reserved not spendable, and unknown · wrong-signer · amount-mismatch · star reserve each refuse whole; the Cord and the fold stand at the door."
